ise the bet.\n\n\n', 'output': 'Evaluation: You hold Ace-Nine offsuit (Ac 9d), which is a strong starting hand in a heads-up matchup (top ~30% of hands). You are likely in the Small Blind position (having posted 50 chips), giving you the advantage of acting last post-flop. Folding is too passive for an Ace. While calling (limping) is an option, raising allows you to take the initiative, build the pot with a likely superior hand, and potentially win the Big Blind immediately. A minimum raise strikes a balance between aggression and pot control given your lead in the overall match.\n\nReason: A9o is a strong heads-up hand worth playing aggressively to utilize position and hand strength. A min-raise is the standard optimal play here.\n\nAnswer: 200'}
